  they measure work done, NOT hardware speed. Do not read them as ARM perf.
  [ref:N rows spread 0..Sq-1]: the fp32 ref checks N rows SPREAD over the whole
  sequence, incl. row Sq-1 -- which attends all Sk keys and so walks every key
  block and every online-softmax rescale. (A prefix of N rows would be causal-
  masked down to an NxN corner of the FIRST key block: same cost, no coverage.)
